\f1\fs22 Shortly before sunrise, the potion Chilo had slipped Sarah stirred not only her dream state but parts distinctly corporeal. She squirmed and tossed, breathing heavily, as a dream lover ravished her. She moaned as he targeted her breast, sucking hungrily, as if he\'92d never been weaned. In slack-mouthed gratification, Sarah looked down and saw\'85 Chanta, latched to her chest raisin.\
She woke instantly. Chanta was snoring beside her, facing away. Yet the sucking sensation persisted. Sarah\'92s horror tripled when she found that disc, which she\'92d hidden in her bra, now alive and glued to her nipple, transforming into a carnivorous slug intent on turning her tit into breakfast. She recoiled, flicked at it. It stayed stuck, stubborn as an Elvis impersonator\'92s hair gel. She squealed, which jolted Chanta awake.\
\'93What the tax?\'94 Chanta gaped at Sarah\'92s writhing horror.\
\'93Get it off! Get it off!\'94 Sarah shrieked.\
Chanta tried to pry free the disc but found no clean edge; the thing had melted, fusing to her flesh. \'93It\'92s stuck!\'94 Panic rising, he worked his fingers in. 
\f2\i Nice, flat belly, too.
\f1\i0 \
Sarah stifled a rising wail. \'93Just pull it off me, please! Before it buries under my skin.\'94 \
Chanta straddled her, gripped round the disc, and just as it cooled and solidified, managed to peel it off.\
Sarah exhaled, the colour flooding back to her face. Had she not been gasping for breath, she would have said exactly what Chanta did: \'93Oh, thank tax!\'94\
Chanta suddenly bellowed, wide-eyed, as the disc latched on to his hand. An involuntary spasm sent his arm jerking until the disc finally let go; it sailed across the room and smacked the wall near the door.\
The wall shook, the door rattled, the floor wobbled, the bed shuddered, windows buzzed, and a cascade of dust rained down on the bed.\
Chanta coughed. \'93Jesus taxing Christ.\'94 He flopped on the mattress beside Sarah. \'93What is that thing?\'94\
Sarah swallowed hard and coughed up dust.\
\'93We gotta get rid of it,\'94 Chanta said, rolling on his back. \'93Just leave it here.\'94\
\'93We can\'92t,\'94 Sarah whimpered.\
\'93Why the tax not?\'94\
\'93Agent Jones wants it. He\'92ll never believe we just threw it away. He\'92ll kill us.\'94\
\'93He\'92ll kill us anyway. Probably donate our minced bodies to FitzBurgers.\'94\
Sarah wept. Chanta repressed his own tears, nurturing whatever cancer best feeds on machismo.\
